---
/**
 * The small uppercase label that sits above a section heading.
 *
 * It is a primitive because it has four callers, not in anticipation of one —
 * the rule ARCHI §11 sets for this directory. Four identical copies of the same
 * scoped rule was the alternative, and the first divergence in letter-spacing
 * would have been invisible until two bands sat side by side.
 *
 * It is deliberately not a heading. An eyebrow is a label for the heading
 * beneath it; marking it up as one would put a second, competing heading into
 * the document outline at every band.
 */
---

<p class="eyebrow"><slot /></p>

<style>
  /* `color: inherit` is load-bearing: the eyebrow renders on all three Section
     surfaces, and a fixed colour would fail contrast on the inverted one. */
  .eyebrow {
    color: inherit;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
</style>
